The query in ```plaintext
1result.sql
``` is the best choice because it  

• finds the WA ZIP centroids within the required 5‑mile radius with ST_DWithin,  
• proportionally allocates tract population and income to each intersecting ZIP by exact area ratios,  
• aggregates to total population and computes the average individual income, rounded as requested, and  
• does so with a clear two‑CTE structure that is both correct and simpler than the alternatives (no redundant filtering or extra divisions).